  "description": "SunEditor before 3.4.0 contains a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability because the html.clean() sanitizer's _normalizeURL() function decodes named entities like &colon; to an empty string. Attackers can inject href values such as javascript&colon; that pass the _isSafeURL() check but are decoded by browsers, executing JavaScript when victims click stored links.",
